# FEASIBILITY PROBE grammar — not the extraction grammar (that is Devansh's,
# in /src/extraction, CLAUDE.md §15).
#
# The naive reading of the claim in CLAUDE.md §5: "a hand-written grammar
# constrains a date field to \d{2}/\d{2}/\d{4} at the token level".
#
# It does exactly that, and that turns out not to be enough — see date-valid.gbnf.
root   ::= "{" ws "\"deadline\":" ws date ws "}"
date   ::= "\"" d d "/" d d "/" d d d d "\""
d      ::= [0-9]
ws     ::= [ \t\n]*
